  "seoTitle": "Prabowo Subianto To Propose Two VP Candidates To MPR",
  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo Subianto is scheduled to present two candidates for vice president to the MPR on November 25 to succeed Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto is set to formally submit two vice presidential candidate names to the MPR on November 25.",
    "Verification officials have proposed that candidates must commit to the full selection process and be prohibited from withdrawing.",
    "Suggestions have been made for the two nominees to present their respective visions and missions directly before the MPR assembly."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The process to select a replacement for Gibran Rakabuming Raka as vice president continues as President Prabowo Subianto prepares to submit two nominees to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR). The submission is scheduled for November 25, marking a significant step in the succession process. Within the legislative body, verification team members have urged that both candidates remain committed to the entire selection process, emphasizing that neither should be allowed to withdraw, as such an action could invalidate the requirement for a two-candidate contest. Furthermore, there are calls for these potential successors to present their ideas and vision for the country during an MPR session to ensure transparency. While various names have surfaced in public discourse, including political figures and professionals, no official decision has been finalized to fill the position.",
